From 5a0b8bc3d883ccdfbb6cd28af6438954ad9de5a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toufik Saouchi <toufik.saouchi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:22:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] test(evaluation): repeated routing runs and
 provider-failure resilience

Routing
- Run every routing case EVAL_REPEATS times (default 3), each from a fresh
  conversation; the score is the mean over completed runs and the report
  shows runs fully correct and flags flaky cases.
- Pool routing metrics over every scored turn: intent accuracy and
  confusions, route exact match and the step where a route first leaves
  the expected path, outcome and tool-sequence accuracy, broken workflow
  rules.
- Add six routing probes at the boundaries of the intent rules.

Resilience
- Classify provider failures (retryable LangChain/OpenAI/httpx errors,
  5xx/429, timeouts, open circuit breaker, MCP transport failures folded
  into tool results) apart from agent mistakes.
- Retry a run from a fresh conversation with backoff and jitter, waiting
  out an open breaker; give up as unscored, never as failed.
- Retry DeepEval judge calls that fail or return unreadable JSON.
- Preflight the model and check the toolbox offers every expected tool;
  declare the provider down after runs in a row give up and skip the rest.
- Mark the run INCONCLUSIVE (non-zero exit) when too much is unscored.

